{"name":"Speaking of the Devil","hex":"#a8415b","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"speaking of the devil","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Phrase","definitions":["An expression sometimes used when a person mentioned in the current conversation happens to arrive on the scene."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/speaking_of_the_devil"}],"entries":[{"title":"Speaking of the Devil","blocks":[{"text":"Speaking of the Devil is a 1991 Italian comedy film directed by Enzo Barboni. It was the last collaboration between Barboni and Bud Spencer with the pairs sons co-writing the film together; Spencer's daughter also plays a role in the film."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/bf/Speaking-of-the-devil-poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Speaking_of_the_Devil"},{"title":"Speech","blocks":[{"text":"Speech is the use of the human voice as a medium for language. Spoken language combines vowel and consonant sounds to form units of meaning like words, which belong to a language's lexicon. There are many different intentional speech acts, such as informing, declaring, asking, persuading, directing; acts may vary in various aspects like enunciation, intonation, loudness, and tempo to convey meaning. Individuals may also unintentionally communicate aspects of their social position through speech, such as sex, age, place of origin, physiological and mental condition, education, and experiences."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9f/Real-time_MRI_-_Speaking_%28English%29.ogv/250px--Real-time_MRI_-_Speaking_%28English%29.ogv.jpg","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Speech"},{"title":"Devil","blocks":[{"text":"The devil is a mythical personification of evil as conceived in various cultures and religious traditions. It is seen as the objectification of a hostile and destructive force. Jeffrey Burton Russell states that the different conceptions of the Devil can be summed up as 1. a principle of evil independent from God, 2. an aspect of God, 3. a created being turning evil or 4. a symbol of human evil."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/022_devil_representation.JPG/330px-022_devil_representation.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Devil"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/BlueAngel.png/120px-BlueAngel.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/BlueAngel.png/250px-BlueAngel.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/BlueAngel.png/120px-BlueAngel.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Excerpt of a Byzantine-Mosaic-Image. A blue angel, probably representing the Devil, standing before goats. Early 6th century.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlueAngel.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Nuremberg_chronicles_-_Devil_and_Woman_on_Horseback_%28CLXXXIXv%29.jpg/500px-Nuremberg_chronicles_-_Devil_and_Woman_on_Horseback_%28CLXXXIXv%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Nuremberg_chronicles_-_Devil_and_Woman_on_Horseback_%28CLXXXIXv%29.jpg/1280px-Nuremberg_chronicles_-_Devil_and_Woman_on_Horseback_%28CLXXXIXv%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ae/Nuremberg_chronicles_-_Devil_and_Woman_on_Horseback_%28CLXXXIXv%29.jpg/500px-Nuremberg_chronicles_-_Devil_and_Woman_on_Horseback_%28CLXXXIXv%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Devil on horseback. Nuremberg Chronicle (1493).","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANuremberg_chronicles_-_Devil_and_Woman_on_Horseback_(CLXXXIXv).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/God_and_Lucifer_-_The_Queen_Mary_Psalter_%281310-1320%29%2C_f.1v_-_BL_Royal_MS_2_B_VII.jpg/500px-God_and_Lucifer_-_The_Queen_Mary_Psalter_%281310-1320%29%2C_f.1v_-_BL_Royal_MS_2_B_VII.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d5/God_and_Lucifer_-_The_Queen_Mary_Psalter_%281310-1320%29%2C_f.1v_-_BL_Royal_MS_2_B_VII.jpg/500px-God_and_Lucifer_-_The_Queen_Mary_Psalter_%281310-1320%29%2C_f.1v_-_BL_Royal_MS_2_B_VII.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"God and Lucifer – The Queen Mary Psalter (1310–1320), f.1v – BL Royal MS 2 B VII","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGod_and_Lucifer_-_The_Queen_Mary_Psalter_(1310-1320)%2C_f.1v_-_BL_Royal_MS_2_B_VII.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/La_tenture_de_lApocalypse_%28Angers%29_%282%29.jpg/500px-La_tenture_de_lApocalypse_%28Angers%29_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/La_tenture_de_lApocalypse_%28Angers%29_%282%29.jpg/1280px-La_tenture_de_lApocalypse_%28Angers%29_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/eb/La_tenture_de_lApocalypse_%28Angers%29_%282%29.jpg/500px-La_tenture_de_lApocalypse_%28Angers%29_%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Satan (the dragon; on the left) gives to the beast of the sea (on the right) power represented by a sceptre in a detail of panel III.40 of the medieval French Apocalypse Tapestry, produced between 1377 and 1382