depicted as having grotesque faces and bodies","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADevils-from-Rila-monastery.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Backer_Judgment_%28detail%29.JPG/500px-Backer_Judgment_%28detail%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Backer_Judgment_%28detail%29.JPG/500px-Backer_Judgment_%28detail%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Horns of a goat and a ram, goat's fur and ears, nose and canines of a pig; a typical depiction of the devil in Christian art. The goat, ram and pig are consistently associated with the devil.[65] Detail of a 16th-century painting by Jacob de Backer in the National Museum in Warsaw.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABacker_Judgment_(detail).JPG"}],"sounds":{"speaking of the devil":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/0c/En-au-speak_of_the_devil.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/0/0c/En-au-speak_of_the_devil.ogg/En-au-speak_of_the_devil.ogg.mp3"}]}}}